					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cumaeansibyl" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(456737); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=456737&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609818700" alt="CumaeanSibyl" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=456737)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cumaeansibyl" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(456737); return false;" >CumaeanSibyl</a></span> <span class="odate time_1450637565 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Dec 2015 18:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2427323">
									

<p>It does feel like poorly-translated bootleg software, which makes me wonder if there's an original program in a different language somewhere &#8212; and what other functions that program might have. I'd expect the bootleg version to have missing or badly-translated commands, for instance, so that the lammasu might be capable of other, stranger things if we only knew what the commands were.</p>
<p>Also, this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Punish D-3515 is possible.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The user enters &quot;burn d-3515&quot; in response, but what would happen if they entered &quot;punish d-3515&quot;? Could be the same, could be <em>much</em> different.</p>
<p>And that's why I like this one.</p>

							</div>

								
					
